  <prompt>
    Create the standalone **All-Communications page** (FR-11) — Surface 2 of R2. It is a thin ~50-line Code Page shell at `src/solutions/sprk_communicationspage/` that copies `src/solutions/sprk_invoicespage/src/main.tsx` verbatim except for the config GUID and title, mounting the shipped `<DataGridPageShell>` from `@spaarke/ui-components` pointed at the existing "Active Communications" grid config.

    Requirements:
    - **~50-line shell** — copy `sprk_invoicespage/src/main.tsx`: import `DataGridPageShell` from `@spaarke/ui-components`, set `CONFIG_ID` to the communications grid config, render the shell inside `createRoot(...).render(<React.StrictMode><App/></React.StrictMode>)`. Unlike the invoices page (which is a matter-scoped drill-through), the All-Communications page is GLOBAL — it needs no `parentContext` (omit the matter-id parsing, or pass `parentContext={undefined}`). No business logic lives here.
    - **Bind to grid config `e1826c4c-9575-f111-ab0e-7ced8ddc4a05`** — the shipped "Active Communications" `sprk_gridconfiguration` (entity `sprk_communication`). REUSE it; do NOT create a second default config for `sprk_communication` (NFR-05). Copy the GUID exactly from `spec.md` (FR-11 / §Scope Surface 2).
    - **Register in `scripts/Deploy-AllDataGridConsumers.ps1`** — add the new page to the deploy script's consumer list alongside `sprk_invoicespage` and the other DataGrid Code Pages, so it builds + deploys with the rest.
    - **Widget/launcher only — NO permanent sitemap entry in R2** (owner Q-B). Ship the shell + the deploy-script registration; the page is reached via the widget/launcher/deep link. Do NOT add a sitemap/app-navigation entry — that is deferred to a later config pass.

    §11: no communications standalone page exists today (investigation §3) — this is a new ~50-line shell that copies the invoicespage pattern; the only concrete cost-of-doing-nothing is that there is no standalone All-Communications entry point (spec req 4, the grid half). Do NOT rebuild the grid framework or add a colliding second grid config.
  </prompt>

